*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* XABLOKS  -  ESA/390 CHANNEL SUBSYSTEM CONTROL BLOCKS                *
*                                                                     *
* CP HAS NO DEFINITION OF ANY OF THESE.  BEFORE THIS MEMBER, THE ONLY *
* ORB, IRB AND SCHIB IN THE PROJECT WERE BYTE CONSTANTS POKED INTO    *
* STORAGE BY THE BARE-METAL TESTS, WHICH IS FINE FOR A TEST AND NOT   *
* FINE FOR CP: HAND-CODED DISPLACEMENTS INTO A CONTROL BLOCK ARE      *
* EXACTLY THE PATTERN OF RISK R-01, WHERE SEVENTY BARE LITERALS       *
* ENCODE THE PAGE AND SEGMENT GEOMETRY AND NO SYMBOL RENAME CAN FIND  *
* THEM.  SO THE BLOCKS GET NAMES BEFORE ANY CODE USES THEM.           *
*                                                                     *
* EVERY OFFSET AND EVERY BIT BELOW IS TAKEN FROM HERCULES' OWN        *
* esa390.h RATHER THAN FROM MEMORY, BECAUSE HERCULES IS WHAT ACCEPTS  *
* OR REJECTS THE BLOCK.  THE LAYOUTS ARE ARCHITECTED AND ARE          *
* UNCHANGED IN Z/ARCHITECTURE, SO THIS MEMBER CARRIES FORWARD.        *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         SPACE 2
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* ORB  -  OPERATION REQUEST BLOCK.  READ BY SSCH.  WORD ALIGNED.      *
*                                                                     *
* TWELVE BYTES ARE ARCHITECTED.  THIRTY-TWO ARE ALLOCATED: DURING THE *
* BARE-METAL TESTS A TWELVE-BYTE ORB AT THE VERY END OF THE POKED     *
* IMAGE TOOK AN ADDRESSING EXCEPTION ON A FETCH THE ARCHITECTURE SAYS *
* NEVER HAPPENS.  INSIDE AN IOBLOK THAT CANNOT ARISE, BUT THE LARGER  *
* AREA COSTS TWENTY BYTES AND REMOVES THE QUESTION.                   *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
ORBLOK   DSECT
ORBPARM  DS    1F             INTERRUPTION PARAMETER -- CP'S OWN TAG
ORBFLG4  DS    1X             KEY AND SUSPEND CONTROL
ORBFLG5  DS    1X             FORMAT, PREFETCH, INITIAL STATUS
ORBLPM   DS    1X             LOGICAL PATH MASK -- SEE ORBLPMOK
ORBFLG7  DS    1X             SUPPRESS-LENGTH AND EXTENSION CONTROL
ORBCCW   DS    1F             CCW ADDRESS, BIT 0 MUST BE ZERO
         DS    5F             PAD -- SEE THE HEADING ABOVE
ORBSIZE  EQU   *-ORBLOK       THIRTY-TWO BYTES
         SPACE 1
ORB4KEY  EQU   X'F0'          SUBCHANNEL PROTECTION KEY
ORB4S    EQU   X'08'          SUSPEND CONTROL
         SPACE 1
*  ORBCCWFM IS THE PROJECT-WIDE CCW FORMAT.  EVERY PLACE THAT BUILDS
*  AN ORB TAKES FLAG5 FROM HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE, SO THE CHOICE IS
*  MADE ONCE.  ZERO NOW; ORB5F WHEN REAL STORAGE OUTGROWS 16 MB AND
*  THE 240 CCW SITES ARE REBUILT.  A COMMENT SAYING "LEAVE THIS ZERO"
*  IS NOT A PARAMETER, WHICH IS WHY THIS EQU EXISTS.  R-27.
ORBCCWFM EQU   0              CCW FORMAT: 0 NOW, ORB5F LATER
ORB5F    EQU   X'80'          CCW FORMAT 1.  CP MUST LEAVE THIS ZERO:
*  FORMAT 0 IS  CODE, ADDR(3), FLAGS, COUNT  -- THE S/370 CCW LAYOUT,
*  BYTE FOR BYTE.  FORMAT 1 IS  CODE, FLAGS, COUNT, ADDR(4).  BOTH ARE
*  EIGHT BYTES, SO A FORMAT MISMATCH IS NOT A LENGTH ERROR AND NOTHING
*  DIAGNOSES IT: THE COMMAND CODE STILL READS CORRECTLY AND THE FLAGS,
*  COUNT AND DATA ADDRESS ARE ALL TAKEN FROM THE WRONG BYTES.  WITH
*  FORMAT 0 EVERY EXISTING CP CHANNEL PROGRAM WORKS UNCONVERTED, WHICH
*  IS HUNDREDS OF CCWS LEFT ALONE.  THE PRICE IS A 24-BIT CCW DATA
*  ADDRESS, SO CHANNEL PROGRAMS REACH ONLY THE LOW 16 MB -- A GATE TO
*  LIFT WITH FORMAT 1 OR IDAWS WHEN REAL STORAGE GROWS.  R-27.
ORB5P    EQU   X'40'          PREFETCH
ORB5I    EQU   X'20'          INITIAL STATUS INTERRUPTION
ORB5A    EQU   X'10'          ADDRESS LIMIT CHECKING
ORB5U    EQU   X'08'          SUPPRESS SUSPENDED INTERRUPTION
         SPACE 1
ORB7L    EQU   X'80'          SUPPRESS INCORRECT LENGTH
ORB7X    EQU   X'01'          ORB EXTENSION CONTROL
         SPACE 1
*  LPM MUST BE X'80', NOT X'00'.  SSCH TESTS  ORB.LPM & PMCW.PAM  AND
*  PAM IS X'80', SO A ZERO LPM MEANS "NO PATH AVAILABLE" RATHER THAN
*  "ANY PATH" AND SSCH RETURNS CONDITION CODE 3 WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC.
*  THAT COST A DEBUGGING CYCLE IN THE TESTS; IT IS A NAMED CONSTANT
*  HERE SO IT CANNOT COST ANOTHER.
ORBLPMOK EQU   X'80'          THE ONLY CORRECT LPM FOR THIS LAB
         SPACE 2
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* SCSW  -  SUBCHANNEL STATUS WORD.  TWELVE BYTES.  APPEARS INSIDE     *
* BOTH THE IRB (STORED BY TSCH) AND THE SCHIB (STORED BY STSCH).      *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
SCSWLOK  DSECT
SCSWFLG0 DS    1X             KEY, SUSPEND, ESW FORMAT, DEFERRED CC
SCSWFLG1 DS    1X             FORMAT, PREFETCH, INITIAL STATUS, ZERO CC
SCSWFLG2 DS    1X             FUNCTION CONTROL, ACTIVITY CONTROL
SCSWFLG3 DS    1X             ACTIVITY CONTROL, STATUS CONTROL
SCSWCCW  DS    1F             CCW ADDRESS
SCSWDST  DS    1X             DEVICE STATUS     -- BECOMES CSW+4
SCSWSST  DS    1X             SUBCHANNEL STATUS -- BECOMES CSW+5
SCSWCNT  DS    1H             RESIDUAL COUNT    -- BECOMES CSW+6
SCSWSIZE EQU   *-SCSWLOK      TWELVE BYTES
         SPACE 1
SCSW0KEY EQU   X'F0'          SUBCHANNEL PROTECTION KEY
SCSW0S   EQU   X'08'          SUSPEND CONTROL
SCSW0L   EQU   X'04'          ESW FORMAT -- LOGOUT STORED
SCSW0CC  EQU   X'03'          DEFERRED CONDITION CODE
         SPACE 1
SCSW1F   EQU   X'80'          CCW FORMAT
SCSW1I   EQU   X'20'          INITIAL STATUS INTERRUPTION
SCSW1Z   EQU   X'04'          ZERO CONDITION CODE -- SEE BELOW
SCSW1E   EQU   X'02'          EXTENDED CONTROL
SCSW1N   EQU   X'01'          PATH NOT OPERATIONAL
         SPACE 1
*  SCSW1Z IS THE SUBSTITUTE FOR SIO'S SYNCHRONOUS CONDITION CODE.
*  WITH ORB5I SET, THE FIRST STATUS CARRIES SCSW1Z AND A DEFERRED
*  CONDITION CODE OF ZERO IN SCSWFLG0.  PROVEN BY EXECUTION IN
*  tests/hardware/06-initial-status.rc, WHICH IS WHAT RETIRED THE
*  WORRY THAT SSCH HAD NO EQUIVALENT OF SIO'S CONTRACT.
         SPACE 1
SCSW2FC  EQU   X'70'          FUNCTION CONTROL
SCSW2FCS EQU   X'40'          ... START FUNCTION
SCSW2FCH EQU   X'20'          ... HALT FUNCTION
SCSW2FCC EQU   X'10'          ... CLEAR FUNCTION
SCSW2AC  EQU   X'0F'          ACTIVITY CONTROL -- PENDING FUNCTIONS
SCSW2ACR EQU   X'08'          ... RESUME PENDING
SCSW2ACS EQU   X'04'          ... START PENDING
SCSW2ACH EQU   X'02'          ... HALT PENDING
SCSW2ACC EQU   X'01'          ... CLEAR PENDING
         SPACE 1
SCSW3AC  EQU   X'E0'          ACTIVITY CONTROL -- ACTIVE STATES
SCSW3ACS EQU   X'80'          ... SUBCHANNEL ACTIVE
SCSW3ACD EQU   X'40'          ... DEVICE ACTIVE
SCSW3ACP EQU   X'20'          ... SUSPENDED
SCSW3SC  EQU   X'1F'          STATUS CONTROL
SCSW3SCA EQU   X'10'          ... ALERT STATUS
SCSW3SCI EQU   X'08'          ... INTERMEDIATE STATUS
SCSW3SCP EQU   X'04'          ... PRIMARY STATUS
SCSW3SCS EQU   X'02'          ... SECONDARY STATUS
SCSW3SCN EQU   X'01'          ... STATUS PENDING
         SPACE 1
*  "IS THE DEVICE FREE?" -- WHICH IS WHAT DMKIOS ASKS WITH TIO, AND
*  WHICH TSCH CANNOT ANSWER BECAUSE ITS CONDITION CODE 0 MEANS
*  "STATUS WAS PENDING AND IS NOW CLEARED", NEARLY THE OPPOSITE.
*  THE ESA/390 ANSWER IS STSCH FOLLOWED BY A TEST THAT EVERY ACTIVITY
*  AND STATUS BIT IS OFF.  THESE TWO MASKS ARE THAT TEST.
SCSWBUS2 EQU   SCSW2AC        BUSY IF ANY OF THESE IS ON IN FLAG2
SCSWBUS3 EQU   SCSW3AC+SCSW3SC  ... OR ANY OF THESE IN FLAG3
         SPACE 2
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* IRB  -  INTERRUPTION RESPONSE BLOCK.  STORED BY TSCH.  SIXTY-FOUR   *
* BYTES, WORD ALIGNED.  TSCH ALWAYS STORES ALL SIXTY-FOUR, SO THE     *
* AREA CANNOT BE TRIMMED EVEN THOUGH M1 READS ONLY THE SCSW.          *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
IRBLOK   DSECT
IRBSCSW  DS    XL12           SUBCHANNEL STATUS -- MAP SCSWLOK
IRBESW   DS    XL20           EXTENDED STATUS WORD -- SEE BELOW
IRBECW   DS    XL32           EXTENDED CONTROL WORD
IRBSIZE  EQU   *-IRBLOK       SIXTY-FOUR BYTES
         SPACE 1
*  THE ESW AND ERW ARE WHAT REPLACE S/370 CHANNEL LOGOUT, AND THEY
*  BELONG TO THE ERROR-RECOVERY REWRITE -- RISK R-03 -- NOT TO M1.
*  THE CSW SHIM LEAVES CSW BYTE 0 BIT X'04', LOGOUT PENDING, ALWAYS
*  ZERO, SO EVERY  TM CSW,X'04'  IN CP FALLS THROUGH.  THAT LOSES
*  ERROR DETAIL; IT DOES NOT INVENT ANY, WHICH IS THE SAFE DIRECTION.
         SPACE 2
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* SCHIB  -  SUBCHANNEL INFORMATION BLOCK.  STORED BY STSCH, AND ITS   *
* FIRST TWENTY-EIGHT BYTES ARE READ BY MSCH.  FIFTY-TWO BYTES.        *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
SCHIBLOK DSECT
PMCWPARM DS    1F             INTERRUPTION PARAMETER
PMCWFLG4 DS    1X             INTERRUPTION SUBCLASS
PMCWFLG5 DS    1X             ENABLE, LIMIT MODE, VALID
PMCWDEV  DS    1H             DEVICE NUMBER -- THE MAPPING CP NEEDS
PMCWLPM  DS    1X             LOGICAL PATH MASK
PMCWPNOM DS    1X             PATH NOT OPERATIONAL MASK
PMCWLPUM DS    1X             LAST PATH USED MASK
PMCWPIM  DS    1X             PATH INSTALLED MASK
PMCWMBI  DS    1H             MEASUREMENT BLOCK INDEX
PMCWPOM  DS    1X             PATH OPERATIONAL MASK
PMCWPAM  DS    1X             PATH AVAILABLE MASK
PMCWCHP  DS    XL8            CHANNEL PATH IDENTIFIERS
PMCWZONE DS    1X             SIE ZONE
PMCWFL25 DS    1X             FLAG BYTE 25
PMCWFL26 DS    1X             RESERVED -- MUST BE ZERO
PMCWFL27 DS    1X             FLAG BYTE 27
PMCWSIZE EQU   *-SCHIBLOK     TWENTY-EIGHT BYTES, WHAT MSCH READS
SCHIBSCS DS    XL12           SUBCHANNEL STATUS WORD
SCHIBMOD DS    XL12           MODEL DEPENDENT AREA
SCHIBSIZ EQU   *-SCHIBLOK     FIFTY-TWO BYTES
         SPACE 1
PMCW4ISC EQU   X'38'          INTERRUPTION SUBCLASS
PMCW5E   EQU   X'80'          SUBCHANNEL ENABLED -- SEE BELOW
PMCW5V   EQU   X'01'          SUBCHANNEL VALID
         SPACE 1
*  A SUBCHANNEL IS CREATED VALID BUT NOT ENABLED, AND SSCH ON A
*  DISABLED SUBCHANNEL RETURNS CONDITION CODE 3 SILENTLY -- NO
*  EXCEPTION, NO MESSAGE, NOTHING IN ANY LOG.  SO EVERY SUBCHANNEL CP
*  MEANS TO USE HAS TO BE STSCH'D, HAVE PMCW5E TURNED ON IN THE
*  STORED PMCW, AND BE MSCH'D BACK.  READING THE PMCW FIRST ALSO
*  AVOIDS GETTING THE RESERVED BITS OF FLAG4, 26 AND 27 WRONG, EACH
*  OF WHICH IS AN OPERAND EXCEPTION.
*
*  PMCWDEV IS ALSO HOW CP LEARNS WHICH SUBCHANNEL SERVES WHICH
*  DEVICE.  SUBCHANNEL NUMBERS ARE ASSIGNED IN CONFIGURATION ORDER
*  AND ARE NOT DERIVABLE FROM DEVICE ADDRESSES, SO DMKCPI WALKS THE
*  SUBCHANNELS WITH STSCH, MATCHES PMCWDEV AGAINST RDEVADD, AND FILLS
*  IN RDEVSSID.  THAT IS THE SAME THING MVS/XA DID AT IPL.
         SPACE 2
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* HOW THE SHIM MAPS AN SCSW ONTO CP'S CSW AT REAL X'40'               *
*                                                                     *
*     CSW+0  BIT X'04'   LOGOUT PENDING   ALWAYS ZERO -- SEE ABOVE    *
*     CSW+1..3           CCW ADDRESS      FROM SCSWCCW, LESS EIGHT    *
*     CSW+4              DEVICE STATUS    FROM SCSWDST                *
*     CSW+5              SUBCHANNEL STAT  FROM SCSWSST                *
*     CSW+6..7           RESIDUAL COUNT   FROM SCSWCNT                *
*                                                                     *
* WITH THAT, ALL 1,917 CAW AND CSW REFERENCES IN CP KEEP WORKING      *
* UNCHANGED, WHICH IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE SHIM.  IT IS PRECISELY   *
* WHAT HERCULES DOES IN THE OTHER DIRECTION WHEN IT PRESENTS A CSW    *
* TO AN S/370 GUEST.                                                 *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
